  "case_for": "The core workflow — watch public changelogs/specs, diff for caller-visible breaking changes, AST-match affected call sites, generate a codemod or AI-drafted patch, open a PR — is exactly the kind of bounded, tool-augmented pipeline that a solo builder with AI coding agents can assemble in six weeks, and multiple independent solo/small teams (Nalvis, mendapi, ApiPatch, Since.dev) have already proven a working MVP is buildable fast and cheaply, several as apparent one/two-person efforts. Demand is corroborated by numerous unprompted developer posts describing exactly this pain across Stripe, Shopify, Twilio, and OpenAI, and distribution is nearly free via GitHub Marketplace and dev.to, the same channels every competitor is already using to acquire early users.",
